ok><name>YABE, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>When a power supply voltage is changed to one that causes an erroneous detection of a power supply voltage detection circuit; and when power generation capable of charging into a large-capacity secondary power supply is not detected, a voltage detecting operation is inhibited, and, when power generation capable of charging into a large-capacity secondary power supply is detected, a voltage detecting operation is continued.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Lorsque la tension d'une alimentation fluctue de manière à provoquer une détection erronée de la tension par le circuit détecteur de tension, et lorsque la production d'un courant de charge d'une batterie de forte capacité n'est pas détectée, l'opération de détection de tension est interrompue, et quand la production d'un courant de charge d'une batterie de forte capacité est détectée l'opération de détection se poursuit.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>